{
  "configuration_id": "config_051",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_004 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) at 0.5988 acc. Image encoder (imagenet_vit_l > resnet50) and aggregation (transformer > avgpool, implied) are well-established. However, the RNA encoder dimension is under-explored: pca_n2000 works well, scgpt is clearly poor (0.5070), but scvi_n200 has never been tested in the multiprofile multimodal setting. Question: Does scvi_n200, a learned variational RNA encoder, outperform the linear pca_n2000 when paired with the best image encoder and aggregation? This is the single largest untested variable that could push accuracy above 0.599. Why this experiment: config_051 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, concat) holds all known-best components fixed and swaps only the RNA encoder, giving a clean read on whether a richer RNA representation helps. If it matches or beats config_004, it opens a new promising axis; if it underperforms, we confirm pca_n2000 is optimal and can redirect remaining budget to other levers. Expected cost: ~4.5–5.0 GPU hours (transformer aggregation + ViT-L image encoder, comparable to config_004/005), keeping total well within budget."
}

